{"id": "EUVD-2026-76624", "enisaUuid": "cdfc11ed-d1aa-3fae-b161-1f4808c1dfd5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: restart ssc_expire_umount walk after dropping nfsd_ssc_lock\n\nnfsd4_ssc_expire_umount() walks nn->nfsd_ssc_mount_list with\nlist_for_each_entry_safe(ni, tmp, ...).  For each expired entry it\nsets nsui_busy = true, drops nfsd_ssc_lock to run mntput() on the\nsource vfsmount, then reacquires the lock to list_del + kfree the\nentry and continue iterating via the macro's saved tmp pointer.\n\nThe nsui_busy flag protects the current ni from concurrent\nnfsd4_ssc_setup_dul() finders during the lock-drop window, but it\ndoes not pin tmp.  Another nfsd RPC thread that fails its source-\nserver mount and reaches nfsd4_ssc_cancel_dul() will, during that\nsame window, take nfsd_ssc_lock, list_del + kfree its own ssc_umount\nitem, and release the lock.  If that item is the saved tmp of the\nexpire walk, the next iteration dereferences a freed\nnfsd4_ssc_umount_item.\n\nRestart the walk from the head after the mntput() unlock window so\nno saved next pointer survives the lock-drop.  The list is bounded\nby the number of active inter-server source mounts (typically small)\nand the expire delayed-work runs periodically rather than per-IO,\nso the restart is cheap.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:25", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b59029b8f24a99b5d844af2da3950d39d36eeea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9e151fea5ed706c1284adacabd869b0be745db2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/659ee3da073164e1e6e40dfcbc26eeed85845f93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60680ae7243b22de3d09be990d8e23bcfc4af837", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77de363d9a1c8cd35f20482782c612cda085791a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ed8d2317aef21cc2a9e5a55d6b59860b4b151a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7377fa964b8aaf47cb04e5efcc4c82d15e8c2ce9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/036c1b182f4da65363e79ec0ac276edc6b7296e5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89712", "GHSA-cfxc-m2r2-5grw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08c6ab48-9fe7-3849-91cb-592b28b76183", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "0bbac0a2-ee6e-35f6-ac72-aa7cf7c879f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "113ced3b-6212-3e74-8456-759cbd4311bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "174eba73-01c5-3f31-8a04-1b027b224a42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4e44b393389c77958f7c58bf4415032b4cda15b <7377fa964b8aaf47cb04e5efcc4c82d15e8c2ce9"}, {"id": "190ee419-d02d-3e46-abcf-97e444d6ccfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "1ef6a2b0-833c-3797-8dc2-921b1448ad1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "276fc825-f417-31bc-a90a-ef6167e397f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "2aba59c3-94c2-3312-80c4-bf008ed09e20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4e44b393389c77958f7c58bf4415032b4cda15b <659ee3da073164e1e6e40dfcbc26eeed85845f93"}, {"id": "31e005f4-e2fd-3ad7-b773-46971a6d4614", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f4e44b393389c77958f7c58bf4415032b4cda15b <d9e151fea5ed706c1284adacabd869b0be745db2"}, {"id": "3ff4381a-2972-3f7c-9f0e-a398e839629a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "437e0578-6616-3b49-a7f0-6c8063fa55e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}